```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

void vulnerableFunction(char *str) {
    char buffer[10];
    // Copy the input string into the buffer without checking its length
    strcpy(buffer, str);
}

int main() {
    char userInput[50];
    printf("Enter your input: ");
    fgets(userInput, 50, stdin);  // Read user input
    // Call the vulnerable function with user input
    vulnerableFunction(userInput);
    return 0;
}
```

In this example, `vulnerableFunction` uses `strcpy` to copy an input string into a fixed-size buffer (`buffer`). If the input string is longer than the buffer size (10 bytes), the excess characters will overwrite whatever is in the memory immediately following the buffer.

